Recompiler: lq and sq align the address down to a multiple of 16, like the reference.

What it fixes: OPCODE_LQ / OPCODE_SQ were translated with READ128 / WRITE128 of the plain address sum, so an
address that is not a multiple of 16 read or wrote the 16 bytes starting at that address. The reference
emulator's interpreter (third_party/pcsx2/pcsx2/R5900OpcodeImpl.cpp, Interpreter::OpcodeImpl::LQ at :747 and SQ
at :872) clears the low four bits of the address first, as the R5900 does (no address error for lq/sq). The
generated code now masks the register-based address with & ~0xFu. A constant address resolved from a lui/ori pair
(memory hint) is not touched: a literal that is not a multiple of 16 in an lq/sq is not expected.

How it was verified: the conformance tests of family "memory" (lq, sq, form "unaligned address": 24 cases each
at offsets 1, 4, 8 and 15 inside the 16 bytes) fail without this change and pass with a recompiler relinked with
it (pytest command of tests/conformance, see journal 025). Whether the game has an lq/sq on an unaligned address
is not known; compilers emit them aligned, so the change is expected to be a no-op for the game. Apply it only
together with a regeneration and a regression run.

Original work for this repository (no code from another project).

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
index 7684097..0a2d7a4 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
@@ -196,9 +196,9 @@ namespace ps2recomp
         case OPCODE_SW:
             return genWrite(32, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_U32(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
         case OPCODE_LQ:
-            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
+            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {}) & ~0xFu", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
         case OPCODE_SQ:
-            return genWrite(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_VEC(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
+            return genWrite(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {}) & ~0xFu", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_VEC(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
         case OPCODE_LD:
             return fmt::format("SET_GPR_U64(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(64, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
